Are you. uh… are you going back there or…

253
00:15:06.405 --> 00:15:10.034
No. uh. my mom's gonna go.
I'm working at Tony's tonight.

254
00:15:10.743 --> 00:15:11.577
Right.

255
00:15:12.745 --> 00:15:13.704
Yeah.

256
00:15:15.831 --> 00:15:16.957
Yeah.

257
00:15:17.041 --> 00:15:18.125
So.

258
00:15:19.793 --> 00:15:21.128
uh. I'll see you.

259
00:15:21.211 --> 00:15:23.088
Yes. Yeah. Bye.

260
00:15:23.172 --> 00:15:24.381
Bye.

261
00:15:29.595 --> 00:15:31.347
Hey. You ready to go?

262
00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:33.891
I… I have to go take Parker to football.

263
00:15:33.974 --> 00:15:36.810
-So. uh. I'll see you tomorrow?
-Yeah. I mean. I'm always here. so…

264
00:15:36.894 --> 00:15:37.728
Sure thing.

265
00:15:38.228 --> 00:15:39.855
- Bye. Jackie.
- See ya.

266
00:15:39.939 --> 00:15:41.065
See ya.

267
00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:45.694
What was up with that?

268
00:15:46.737 --> 00:15:47.613
Mmm.

269
00:15:47.696 --> 00:15:50.032
Uh-huh. No. come here! Grace!

270
00:15:55.287 --> 00:15:57.539
-Here's that pizza for you.
-Thank you.

271
00:15:58.415 --> 00:15:59.333
Here you guys go.

272
00:15:59.416 --> 00:16:00.626
Hey!

273
00:16:01.752 --> 00:16:03.170
Oh my God.

274
00:16:08.217 --> 00:16:09.718
- Thank you so much.
- Hey. Kiley.

275
00:16:10.386 --> 00:16:13.347
Kiley. Kiley. hey.
Still worried about this?

276
00:16:14.807 --> 00:16:17.393
You know. being talked about
is actually considered a perk

277
00:16:17.476 --> 00:16:19.770
of being
the former football captain's girlfriend.

278
00:16:20.562 --> 00:16:23.607
-It's a bit like being famous. I guess.
-I don't want to be famous.

279
00:16:25.693 --> 00:16:26.527
Right.

280
00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:30.823
It's fine. No. I'm… I'm fine. Uh…

281
00:16:31.323 --> 00:16:33.033
Just go be with your friends.

282
00:16:35.577 --> 00:16:36.495
Okay.

283
00:16:37.079 --> 00:16:39.331
<i>♪ Though nothing to say…♪</i>

284
00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:47.047
Do you think we need
to save some for Alex and Cole?

285
00:16:47.131 --> 00:16:49.258
Honestly. I think they dodged a bullet.

286
00:16:49.341 --> 00:16:50.426
Who sent this one?

287
00:16:50.509 --> 00:16:52.803
Pete Weber brought it
when he brought Custard back.

288
00:16:52.886 --> 00:16:53.929
What is it?

289
00:16:54.013 --> 00:16:55.347
Grey.

290
00:16:56.015 --> 00:16:57.224
Is it eggplant?

291
00:16:58.475 --> 00:16:59.309
I hope so.

292
00:16:59.393 --> 00:17:01.520
God. what is this?

293
00:17:02.229 --> 00:17:03.063
Ugh.

294
00:17:03.814 --> 00:17:05.107
Here you go. bud.

295
00:17:07.192 --> 00:17:08.527
And I forgot napkins.

296
00:17:09.403 --> 00:17:13.490
The website said that heavier smoothies
are easier for him to swallow.

297
00:17:13.574 --> 00:17:16.535
so this has chia seeds in it.
as well as hemp and avocado.

298
00:17:16.618 --> 00:17:19.121
Perfect. I will deliver that.

299
00:17:19.663 --> 00:17:21.206
But I might not mention the hemp.

300
00:17:21.707 --> 00:17:22.541
Or the chia.

301
00:17:23.751 --> 00:17:26.336
You know. I'm gonna head over
to the hospital in a little bit.

302
00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:28.422
if you wanna… join me.

303
00:17:29.089 --> 00:17:32.426
Yeah. I mean. I would love to.
but I already told Danny I would babysit.

304
00:17:33.844 --> 00:17:34.720
Cool.

305
00:17:35.763 --> 00:17:36.889
I'll say hi for you.

306
00:17:36.972 --> 00:17:38.015
Okay.

307
00:17:43.937 --> 00:17:45.397
Cole.

308
00:17:45.481 --> 00:17:47.316
Come here. I wanna show you something.

309
00:17:51.278 --> 00:17:52.613
Pretty special. right?

310
00:17:54.782 --> 00:17:56.658
This is KC Mackindson's car.

311
00:17:58.035 --> 00:17:59.203
Mac's a drag racer.

312
00:17:59.703 --> 00:18:00.913
Brought her in last night.

313
00:18:00.996 --> 00:18:04.291
Said the… the timing was weird
in his last race.

314
00:18:04.875 --> 00:18:06.168
Thinks something's off.

315
00:18:06.752 --> 00:18:08.128
I've known Mac for years.

316
00:18:08.629 --> 00:18:10.005
He's got a lot of cars.

317
00:18:10.756 --> 00:18:12.758
So he's an important customer for us.

318
00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:16.053
Well. I… I can take a look.

319
00:18:16.678 --> 00:18:17.513
Yeah?

320
00:18:18.013 --> 00:18:18.847
Yeah.

321
00:18:19.681 --> 00:18:20.599
I'd like to fix her.

322
00:18:20.682 --> 00:18:21.517
Okay.

323
00:18:22.017 --> 00:18:22.851
Great.

324
00:18:23.519 --> 00:18:24.478
I'll let Mac know.

325
00:18:39.576 --> 00:18:41.995
Hey. what are you doing here?
I thought you were babysitting.

326
00:18:42.079 --> 00:18:44.206
Yeah. Jackie decided to stay home.

327
00:18:44.832 --> 00:18:48.377
And honestly. I…
I just wanted to get out of the house.

328
00:18:48.877 --> 00:18:51.797
You know. it's…
it's not really the same without. uh…

329
00:18:52.422 --> 00:18:54.258
Hold on. Where… where were you going?

330
00:18:54.842 --> 00:18:56.677
I was coming to see you.

331
00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:58.345
{\an8}With this.

332
00:18:58.846 --> 00:19:00.055
I got it from the library.

333
00:19:00.139 --> 00:19:02.432
I wanted you to feel like
you were back in New York again

334
00:19:02.516 --> 00:19:04.101
to take your mind off everything.

335
00:19:04.184 --> 00:19:06.562
Plus. no shade.
but I think Jane Fonda and Robert Redford

336
00:19:06.645 --> 00:19:08.814
might just have the edge
on Miss Calvert. the lunch lady.

337
00:19:08.897 --> 00:19:10.607
and Elwin from the gas station.

338
00:19:12.067 --> 00:19:13.068
Thank you.

339
00:19:14.486 --> 00:19:16.321
Come in. You hungry? My mom made dinner.

340
00:19:16.405 --> 00:19:18.532
Oh. thank God. Yes.

341
00:19:18.615 --> 00:19:21.451
I couldn't face another
of Ma Weber's casseroles.

342
00:19:36.758 --> 00:19:37.676
Kiley.

343
00:19:38.635 --> 00:19:39.553
Hey.

344
00:19:40.053 --> 00:19:42.014
Come on.
I cannot believe you of all people

345
00:19:42.097 --> 00:19:44.099
care what kids at school think or say.

346
00:19:44.183 --> 00:19:46.768
I mean. you think most of them are idiots.

347
00:19:48.645 --> 00:19:51.190
All my life. I've been under the radar.

348
00:19:51.732 --> 00:19:53.150
Okay? And that's how I like it.

349
00:19:55.527 --> 00:19:56.403
Okay.

350
00:19:57.196 --> 00:19:59.406
Everybody's talking about us. Dylan.

351
00:20:01.283 --> 00:20:02.242
So?

352
00:20:02.326 --> 00:20:04.161
So?

353
00:20:04.244 --> 00:20:07.080
It's not like they're talking about
how I can do better. are they?

354
00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:15.255
Just… …don't worry about it.

355
00:20:17.007 --> 00:20:19.301
They're gonna get bored eventually.
I promise.

356
00:20:19.384 --> 00:20:23.764
Yeah. but what if you start
to think that you could do better too?

357
00:20:27.559 --> 00:20:28.435
Please.

358
00:20:31.146 --> 00:20:34.524
If anybody is gonna wake up
and realize they can do better…

359
00:20:36.526 --> 00:20:37.527
it's gonna be you.

360
00:20:39.738 --> 00:20:42.157
I don't care what anyone thinks. Kiley.

361
00:21:03.804 --> 00:21:05.222
Hey. guys!

362
00:21:06.056 --> 00:21:08.684
Everybody! I made brunch!

363
00:21:17.109 --> 00:21:18.193
Oh.

364
00:21:18.277 --> 00:21:19.444
Wow!

365
00:21:20.070 --> 00:21:20.946
Look at this.

366
00:21:21.029 --> 00:21:23.532
Yeah. well. we've all been so…

367
00:21:24.032 --> 00:21:26.576
It's been so long
since we all sat down together.

368
00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:28.412
I thought it'd be good for us
to have brunch.

369
00:21:28.495 --> 00:21:29.413
All of us.

370
00:21:29.496 --> 00:21:31.665
Oh. man. there's nothing I'd love more.

371
00:21:31.748 --> 00:21:35.460
but I've got a bunch of appointments.
which I would cancel in a heartbeat. but

372
00:21:36.044 --> 00:21:38.213
I've been so behind
because of the hospital.

373
00:21:38.797 --> 00:21:39.631
I'm sorry.

374
00:21:39.715 --> 00:21:40.590
It's okay.

375
00:21:40.674 --> 00:21:42.259
This looks amazing.

376
00:21:42.342 --> 00:21:44.386
-Did you make those?
-Mm-hmm.

377
00:21:44.469 --> 00:21:47.055
From scratch. I wanted it to feel special.

378
00:21:47.139 --> 00:21:48.390
It is special.

379
00:21:49.266 --> 00:21:50.100
Thank you.

380
00:21:50.183 --> 00:21:52.686
Oh. uh. before I forget.
I made a smoothie for George.

381
00:21:52.769 --> 00:21:54.771
-It's in the fridge.
-Great! I'll grab it.

382
00:21:55.355 --> 00:21:56.732
-Have fun!
-Thanks.

383
00:21:56.815 --> 00:21:58.775
Parker! You can sit here.

384
00:21:58.859 --> 00:22:01.945
Uh. I'm okay.
I'm actually gonna go watch TV.

385
00:22:02.029 --> 00:22:03.530
-Right. But. uh…
-Yeah.

386
00:22:04.614 --> 00:22:06.491
Jordan! Do you want some fruit salad?

387
00:22:06.575 --> 00:22:07.909
Yeah. thanks.

388
00:22:08.493 --> 00:22:11.371
- Parker. do not change that channel.
- I will if I get there first!

389
00:22:11.455 --> 00:22:16.710
Hi! There is coffee. hot chocolate.
and I squeezed that juice myself.

390
00:22:17.419 --> 00:22:18.253
Cool.

391
00:22:21.465 --> 00:22:22.424
Okay.

392
00:22:23.508 --> 00:22:25.218
-What is this?
-Um…

393
00:22:25.802 --> 00:22:28.555
Guys. I was kinda hoping we could all sit…

394
00:22:31.600 --> 00:22:33.226
Benny. where are you going?

395
00:22:33.310 --> 00:22:35.729
Oh. I have to go check on Gregory.

396
00:22:37.314 --> 00:22:38.857
This was great. Jackie.

397
00:22:38.940 --> 00:22:39.983
You're leaving?

398
00:22:40.734 --> 00:22:42.444
Uh. I have training.

399
00:22:42.986 --> 00:22:43.862
Okay.

400
00:22:44.905 --> 00:22:46.031
See you.

401
00:22:53.705 --> 00:22:54.664
Cole.

402
00:22:56.291 --> 00:22:57.209
Hey. Cole.

403
00:22:58.085 --> 00:23:00.587
I. uh… I… I made brunch.

404
00:23:01.671 --> 00:23:02.631
Oh.

405
00:23:04.216 --> 00:23:05.133
Right.

406
00:23:06.176 --> 00:23:09.721
Yeah. do you mind
if I take some for the guys?

407
00:23:10.472 --> 00:23:11.431
The guys?

408
00:23:13.016 --> 00:23:14.142
At the shop.

409
00:23:15.018 --> 00:23:17.270
Yeah. I'd stay. really.

410
00:23:17.354 --> 00:23:19.147
but I. um… I'm going to the hospital.

411
00:23:19.231 --> 00:23:21.608
and then I gotta go to work
just after. so…

412
00:23:21.691 --> 00:23:23.110
- Okay.
- Are you leaving?

413
00:23:23.193 --> 00:23:25.612
Could you drop me off at band practice?

414
00:23:25.695 --> 00:23:28.865
Um… Yeah. Yeah. let's go.

415
00:23:28.949 --> 00:23:32.244
-Uh. Nathan. you don't want to eat first?
-Sorry. I'm so late.

416
00:23:37.416 --> 00:23:38.917
Mmm.

417
00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:40.043
Is Danny home?

418
00:23:40.127 --> 00:23:43.296
Uh. no. I don't think so.
I think he stayed at Erin's last night.

419
00:23:44.464 --> 00:23:45.340
Mmm.

420
00:23:46.508 --> 00:23:47.801
It's really good. though.

421
00:23:48.844 --> 00:23:49.719
Thanks.

422
00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:05.485
I'm glad you're here.
How's your dad doing?

423
00:24:05.569 --> 00:24:07.529
Oh. he's fine. He'll be home soon.

424
00:24:08.238 --> 00:24:09.573
Okay. Let's go get ready.

425
00:24:10.073 --> 00:24:11.074
Come on.

426
00:24:14.411 --> 00:24:17.622
Whenever my dad comes to visit me.
it's so… weird.

427
00:24:17.706 --> 00:24:19.499
It's like he thinks
I'm eight years old again.

428
00:24:20.292 --> 00:24:22.711
You know.
last weekend he brought me a lollipop.

429
00:24:22.794 --> 00:24:23.879
I'm sorry. Grace.

430
00:24:23.962 --> 00:24:26.715
No. it's okay. I kinda like lollipops.

431
00:24:31.678 --> 00:24:34.389
I don't know. It's just they both seem
so miserable without each other.

432
00:24:34.473 --> 00:24:36.766
and then no one will tell me
what's going on.

433
00:24:37.684 --> 00:24:38.643
You know?

434
00:24:39.144 --> 00:24:40.228
Anyways.

435
00:24:40.729 --> 00:24:43.815
you've been here like a hundred hours.
and all we've talked about are my parents.

436
00:24:43.899 --> 00:24:47.611
so you owe me a distraction.

437
00:24:48.904 --> 00:24:50.614
What's happening with Alex and Cole?

438
00:24:51.490 --> 00:24:54.576
I guess you guys know
where you stand now. right?

439
00:24:54.659 --> 00:24:55.494
I guess.

440
00:24:55.994 --> 00:24:57.954
I mean. we're all trying to be civil. but

441
00:24:59.039 --> 00:25:03.418
with everything happening with George.
it's like everything is fractured.

442
00:25:05.795 --> 00:25:09.549
No one wants to be
in the same room as anybody else.

443
00:25:11.218 --> 00:25:13.470
Like we're all finding it too hard
to be around each other.

444
00:25:13.553 --> 00:25:15.972
And what about you and Cole?

445
00:25:16.515 --> 00:25:20.936
With George and Alex and Katherine…

446
00:25:22.479 --> 00:25:24.564
If Cole and I got together now. it would

447
00:25:25.065 --> 00:25:26.483
blow up everything.

448
00:25:26.983 --> 00:25:29.319
Like. the whole family. and…

449
00:25:30.820 --> 00:25:34.324
Everybody's been through so much.
It's just not the right time.

450
00:25:36.117 --> 00:25:37.536
Well. are you okay?

451
00:25:38.245 --> 00:25:40.288
I just really wanted
to do something.

452
00:25:40.372 --> 00:25:42.791
If I got the family to feel better

453
00:25:43.416 --> 00:25:45.043
or to feel more normal

454
00:25:45.544 --> 00:25:49.881
then maybe we wouldn't
all be missing George so much.

455
00:25:50.924 --> 00:25:56.471
And then maybe this weirdness between
me. Alex. and Cole wouldn't feel so big.

456
00:25:58.598 --> 00:26:01.351
And then maybe
I wouldn't feel so guilty all the time.

457
00:26:02.394 --> 00:26:05.355
Well. there's only one way to fix that.

458
00:26:06.648 --> 00:26:07.816
You have to talk to them.

459
00:26:09.359 --> 00:26:10.235
Yeah. you're right.

460
00:26:11.653 --> 00:26:13.154
I know you're right.

461
00:26:18.577 --> 00:26:20.537
Hey.

462
00:26:20.620 --> 00:26:21.830
What's going on with Murphy?

463
00:26:21.913 --> 00:26:24.332
Oh yeah.
I think he's a little agitated.

464
00:26:25.041 --> 00:26:27.460
It might be that hoof right there.

465
00:26:28.878 --> 00:26:31.172
Okay. All right. Murphy.

466
00:26:35.010 --> 00:26:36.678
I will take care of that when I get home.

467
00:26:38.972 --> 00:26:40.056
- Mom.
- Yeah?

468
00:26:43.602 --> 00:26:44.894
Are you okay?

469
00:26:45.395 --> 00:26:46.813
Yeah. I'm fine.

470
00:26:49.649 --> 00:26:52.027
I'm a little bit tired. That's all.

471
00:26:54.821 --> 00:26:56.031
See you later.

472
00:26:56.531 --> 00:26:57.532
See ya.

473
00:27:01.244 --> 00:27:05.540
So. this is from Jackie.
She said it's a healthy-fats dessert.

474
00:27:08.168 --> 00:27:09.586
-See you later.
-Yeah.

475
00:27:09.669 --> 00:27:12.297
Can she just not send ice cream? I mean…

476
00:27:15.008 --> 00:27:16.468
-See ya.
-Bye. honey.

477
00:27:16.551 --> 00:27:17.469
Thank you.

478
00:27:18.136 --> 00:27:20.180
Before I go. you guys need anything?

479
00:27:20.847 --> 00:27:21.973
- No.
- You sure?

480
00:27:22.057 --> 00:27:23.266
- Thanks.
- All right.

481
00:27:23.350 --> 00:27:24.934
- Careful going home.
- See you.

482
00:27:26.436 --> 00:27:29.272
You know. Jackie should come by.
I haven't seen her at all.

483
00:27:31.274 --> 00:27:32.817
It's not you. honey.

484
00:27:34.402 --> 00:27:35.570
It's hospitals.

485
00:27:36.738 --> 00:27:40.200
I think being here just brings back…

486
00:27:40.283 --> 00:27:41.785
Oh. Yeah.

487
00:27:41.868 --> 00:27:43.078
- Yeah.
- Sure.

488
00:27:43.787 --> 00:27:46.164
I can't say I'm too big on them
right now either.

489
00:27:48.458 --> 00:27:50.126
-What?
-Nothing.

490
00:27:51.670 --> 00:27:52.837
Honey. what?

491
00:27:55.090 --> 00:27:58.927
I just can't stop thinking about
what if Will hadn't found you.

492
00:28:01.096 --> 00:28:02.097
But he did.

493
00:28:03.181 --> 00:28:04.307
Right?

494
00:28:04.891 --> 00:28:06.893
- That was the worst night of my life.
- Hmm.

495
00:28:11.815 --> 00:28:13.191
I thought I lost you.

496
00:28:14.234 --> 00:28:16.736
Okay. well.
I am not that easy to get rid of.

497
00:28:18.071 --> 00:28:19.322
I can't lose you.

498
00:28:20.156 --> 00:28:22.200
-The kids can't lose you.
-Hey.

499
00:28:22.283 --> 00:28:23.785
You are not losing me.

500
00:28:24.285 --> 00:28:25.120
Okay?

501
00:28:25.870 --> 00:28:27.163
I'm gonna be okay.

502
00:28:28.206 --> 00:28:29.249
I promise.

503
00:28:30.083 --> 00:28:31.751
Come on. I love you.

504
00:28:41.386 --> 00:28:42.429
You okay?

505
00:28:43.138 --> 00:28:44.889
No.

506
00:28:44.973 --> 00:28:46.933
I don't know what I'm doing.

507
00:28:47.517 --> 00:28:49.102
Dad usually does this.

508
00:28:50.103 --> 00:28:54.149
You know what?
I'm just gonna… I'm gonna leave it.

509
00:28:54.232 --> 00:28:55.608
Let Dad look at it when he's home.

510
00:28:56.109 --> 00:28:57.610
Even when he's home. I don't think

511
00:28:57.694 --> 00:29:00.238
he's gonna be able to do anything
for a while.

512
00:29:00.905 --> 00:29:02.866
What? Dad?

513
00:29:03.366 --> 00:29:06.494
Nah. no way. he's gonna sit on that couch
watching TV for more than. like. a day.

514
00:29:06.578 --> 00:29:08.371
-Come on.
-Alex.

515
00:29:10.081 --> 00:29:14.043
You know he almost died. right?
You… you get that?

516
00:29:16.129 --> 00:29:17.338
He has to be okay.

517
00:29:18.339 --> 00:29:19.340
I know. I…

518
00:29:20.383 --> 00:29:22.677
But we gotta get used to things
being different around here.

519
00:29:22.761 --> 00:29:26.639
Mom needs more help.
She… she can't go on like this.

520
00:29:27.307 --> 00:29:28.224
Okay.

521
00:29:30.393 --> 00:29:31.644
And Alex.

522
00:29:32.145 --> 00:29:34.355
- About that night.
- Oh.

523
00:29:34.439 --> 00:29:36.649
-What you heard--
-It's fine. It's fine. I get it.

524
00:29:36.733 --> 00:29:38.610
I… I don't want to talk about it.

525
00:29:40.695 --> 00:29:44.324
Look. you and Jackie can do what you want.
Okay? I'm over it.

526
00:29:47.160 --> 00:29:48.203
Are you okay?

527
00:29:53.374 --> 00:29:54.626
Does it matter?

528
00:29:56.461 --> 00:29:58.171
Would it change anything?

529
00:30:00.215 --> 00:30:02.133
I'm sorry I did this to you.

530
00:30:04.093 --> 00:30:08.264
And you know what?
I'm sorry I feel this way.

531
00:30:11.601 --> 00:30:14.229
But… I love her.

532
00:30:16.147 --> 00:30:18.525
I can't… I can't stop that.

533
00:30:20.276 --> 00:30:21.611
If there was…

534
00:30:21.694 --> 00:30:24.155
-If there was anything I can do to--
-I know.

535
00:30:24.781 --> 00:30:26.074
I know.

536
00:30:29.494 --> 00:30:30.662
I love her too.

537
00:30:32.997 --> 00:30:36.084
But I don't want to be with someone
who wants to be with someone else.

538
00:30:41.297 --> 00:30:42.590
Dad being sick.

539
00:30:43.341 --> 00:30:46.678
getting him better.
that's all that matters right now.

540
00:30:47.262 --> 00:30:48.972
Just make her happy. Okay?

541
00:30:50.515 --> 00:30:51.391
Okay.

542
00:30:59.023 --> 00:31:00.817
Katherine.

543
00:31:01.526 --> 00:31:03.403
- Hi.
- What…

544
00:31:03.945 --> 00:31:05.655
Why are you doing this alone?

545
00:31:07.532 --> 00:31:09.242
That is a great question.

546
00:31:10.910 --> 00:31:13.663
I guess this is now my responsibility.

547
00:31:13.746 --> 00:31:16.207
and I suddenly think
I should be able to fix a fence.

548
00:31:17.709 --> 00:31:19.043
I don't do ranch.

549
00:31:19.127 --> 00:31:23.464
I'm from New Haven. I do kids and puppies.
I birth piglets for a living.

550
00:31:23.548 --> 00:31:26.009
-You could've asked one of us.
-No.

551
00:31:26.092 --> 00:31:30.013
You've all been such a help.
I don't want to burden you with more.

552
00:31:30.096 --> 00:31:32.223
You're not. This is too much.

553
00:31:32.307 --> 00:31:34.475
Yeah. it is.

554
00:31:37.353 --> 00:31:38.271
Are you okay?

555
00:31:38.855 --> 00:31:43.568
Yeah. I just… I hate
that I'm not able to do more to help.

556
00:31:43.651 --> 00:31:45.862
Like. I wish I could fix this.

557
00:31:45.945 --> 00:31:46.946
Me too.

558
00:31:47.655 --> 00:31:50.658
I wish I could fix… any of it.

559
00:31:50.742 --> 00:31:53.244
I couldn't even get everyone
to sit down and eat brunch together.

560
00:31:54.370 --> 00:31:58.291
I think the hardest part for us is…
admitting that we need help.

561
00:31:59.792 --> 00:32:01.961
I just wish I could make it better.

562
00:32:02.879 --> 00:32:04.714
Honey. I know that you've been

563
00:32:05.214 --> 00:32:07.550
avoiding going to the hospital
to see George.

564
00:32:07.634 --> 00:32:09.218
Yeah. um…

565
00:32:10.887 --> 00:32:12.889
Being in a hospital.

566
00:32:13.640 --> 00:32:14.599
it's like…

567
00:32:15.099 --> 00:32:19.020
like the smell and everything.
it's… it's too hard.

568
00:32:20.438 --> 00:32:21.439
I'm really sorry.

569
00:32:21.522 --> 00:32:23.232
Don't apologize.

570
00:32:24.317 --> 00:32:27.654
I am sorry you didn't feel like you could
come to me to help you process this.

571
00:32:28.237 --> 00:32:30.281
- It's not about me.
- Yes. it is.

572
00:32:30.365 --> 00:32:34.035
It's about all of us. We all get to put
ourselves first every once in a while.

573
00:32:35.536 --> 00:32:36.412
Even you.

574
00:32:37.330 --> 00:32:38.164
Okay.

575
00:32:38.247 --> 00:32:39.332
Okay?

576
00:32:40.333 --> 00:32:43.002
-I'll try.
-Okay.

577
00:32:47.215 --> 00:32:48.675
You know what I need?

578
00:32:48.758 --> 00:32:50.218
-What?
-A nap.

579
00:32:51.344 --> 00:32:53.638
Or a smoothie. Do you have any more chia?

580
00:32:54.263 --> 00:32:56.182
- I have so much chia.
- Oh!

581
00:32:56.265 --> 00:32:57.642
- Can we go?
- Yeah.

582
00:33:00.395 --> 00:33:01.896
-Do you want to drive?
-No!

583
00:33:05.316 --> 00:33:08.403
All right. What about the grain order?

584
00:33:08.903 --> 00:33:10.780
Yeah. I… I did it for next month.

585
00:33:10.863 --> 00:33:13.324
And the guy said he'll set it up with you
whenever you're home.

586
00:33:13.408 --> 00:33:14.784
Thanks. Cole.

587
00:33:15.660 --> 00:33:18.538
You know. your mother and Will
won't tell me a thing about the ranch.

588
00:33:19.330 --> 00:33:20.373
Well…

589
00:33:23.042 --> 00:33:24.085
All right.

590
00:33:24.168 --> 00:33:27.714
Now. you need to get out of here.

591
00:33:27.797 --> 00:33:31.551
What? Are… are you good? Do you
need me to get a nurse or something?

592
00:33:31.634 --> 00:33:32.885
No. no. I'm fine.

593
00:33:33.553 --> 00:33:35.513
But you've been spending
too much time here.

594
00:33:36.305 --> 00:33:38.891
I want to be here. Dad.

595
00:33:39.434 --> 00:33:43.688
Hey. you were… you were there with me
with my knee the whole time. I…

596
00:33:45.690 --> 00:33:49.110
-I wanna pay you back and be here for you.
-Look. that's not how it works.

597
00:33:49.193 --> 00:33:51.154
All right? I'm the dad. and that's my job.

598
00:33:51.654 --> 00:33:53.364
You… you wanna pay me back?

599
00:33:53.448 --> 00:33:55.825
Then you… you get out there.
and you live your life.

600
00:33:55.908 --> 00:33:58.161
All right? You don't sit around in here.

601
00:33:58.661 --> 00:34:00.038
All right? I'm good.

602
00:34:00.872 --> 00:34:02.248
All right? That make sense?

603
00:34:04.042 --> 00:34:05.793
-Yeah.
-Then get out.

604
00:34:14.635 --> 00:34:15.636
One more thing.

605
00:34:18.765 --> 00:34:20.683
Oh. way better.

606
00:34:21.184 --> 00:34:22.351
Oh.

607
00:34:27.857 --> 00:34:29.484
That's more like it.

608
00:34:30.943 --> 00:34:33.362
- I'll see you soon.
- Thanks. buddy.

609
00:34:47.877 --> 00:34:48.753
Hey.

610
00:34:49.629 --> 00:34:51.798
Oh. Hi.

611
00:34:54.759 --> 00:34:55.760
You okay?

612
00:34:56.469 --> 00:34:57.386
Yeah.

613
00:34:58.429 --> 00:34:59.305
Are you?

614
00:35:02.308 --> 00:35:04.852
I think I finally get
what things have been like for you.

615
00:35:05.394 --> 00:35:06.354
What do you mean?

616
00:35:08.523 --> 00:35:10.108
I've been so scared

617
00:35:10.733 --> 00:35:12.026
about my dad.

618
00:35:12.652 --> 00:35:14.445
I've been pretending
it's not been happening.

619
00:35:16.656 --> 00:35:18.116
You lost everybody.

620
00:35:19.325 --> 00:35:22.203
And I don't think I really understood
what that meant until now.

621
00:35:25.873 --> 00:35:27.083
How do you do it?

622
00:35:30.211 --> 00:35:32.463
Some days are better than others.

623
00:35:33.047 --> 00:35:33.923
But. uh…

624
00:35:34.924 --> 00:35:39.512
I have more good days than bad now.
so I'm doing okay.

625
00:35:41.180 --> 00:35:42.265
I'm better.

626
00:35:43.516 --> 00:35:44.684
It gets better.

627
00:35:47.228 --> 00:35:48.104
Good.

628
00:35:50.690 --> 00:35:51.524
Alex.

629
00:35:52.024 --> 00:35:54.944
you know.
I… I never meant to hurt you. right?

630
00:35:55.027 --> 00:35:57.572
- Or lie to you.
- Yeah. I know.

631
00:35:59.740 --> 00:36:02.869
And even if you weren't lying to me.
you were definitely lying to yourself.

632
00:36:03.494 --> 00:36:04.453
Yeah.

633
00:36:05.788 --> 00:36:08.499
But I'm…
I'm so sorry you heard it like that.

634
00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:10.793
Yeah. that was. uh…

635
00:36:12.003 --> 00:36:15.298
Hearing you tell him you loved him
after you said you loved me.

636
00:36:15.381 --> 00:36:18.217
- I did. I do. I--
- It's not the same though. right?

637
00:36:20.386 --> 00:36:21.721
As it is with Cole.

638
00:36:23.222 --> 00:36:24.307
No.

639
00:36:24.390 --> 00:36:27.018
No. it's… it's not the same.

640
00:36:28.603 --> 00:36:29.562
But. uh…

641
00:36:30.229 --> 00:36:32.064
But being with you was really good.

642
00:36:32.148 --> 00:36:33.357
No. I mean it.

643
00:36:33.858 --> 00:36:38.404
Alex. you are so sweet.
and you were such a great boyfriend.

644
00:36:40.239 --> 00:36:41.824
A lot of the time. though.

645
00:36:42.700 --> 00:36:45.244
it felt like we were trying really hard.

646
00:36:46.746 --> 00:36:47.788
Yeah. I guess.

647
00:36:49.415 --> 00:36:51.250
I don't think
it's supposed to feel like that.

648
00:36:53.502 --> 00:36:54.545
No. you're right.

649
00:36:55.046 --> 00:36:56.923
I guess we both
just had to figure that out.

650
00:37:00.301 --> 00:37:02.178
When did you get to be so wise?

651
00:37:04.722 --> 00:37:08.517
I think my dad and everything
has really showed me what matters.

652
00:37:10.436 --> 00:37:12.939
Hey. you don't gotta look so worried.

653
00:37:14.523 --> 00:37:15.483
I'm gonna be okay.

654
00:37:16.359 --> 00:37:17.360
You are?

655
00:37:17.443 --> 00:37:19.570
I'm a rodeo star now. right?

656
00:37:20.279 --> 00:37:21.864
Girls are gonna be all over me.

657
00:37:21.948 --> 00:37:23.491
Oh. is that right?

658
00:37:24.200 --> 00:37:25.326
That's the plan.

659
00:37:27.870 --> 00:37:30.373
…still hitting the track. huh?

660
00:37:30.456 --> 00:37:33.125
Cole. Hey. Cole.

661
00:37:33.626 --> 00:37:34.919
-This is Mac.
-Hey.

662
00:37:35.002 --> 00:37:37.630
Mac. like I told you.
Cole's the best we have.

663
00:37:37.713 --> 00:37:39.590
If he can't knock her into shape.
nobody can.

664
00:37:39.674 --> 00:37:41.175
I'm glad to hear it.

665
00:37:41.676 --> 00:37:43.594
I gotta get back out there. so…

666
00:37:43.678 --> 00:37:45.680
-Missing the rush. huh?
-Yeah.

667
00:37:45.763 --> 00:37:47.056
When you're racing.

668
00:37:47.139 --> 00:37:50.935
the speed. the crowd.
the smell of the gas.

669
00:37:51.018 --> 00:37:54.563
the fact that you could die at any second.
I'm telling you. there's nothing like it.

670
00:37:56.190 --> 00:37:59.068
Hey. don't you give him any ideas.
I need you here.

671
00:38:00.611 --> 00:38:03.322
So. you like cars.

672
00:38:03.823 --> 00:38:04.949
Hell. you'd love it.

673
00:38:05.533 --> 00:38:08.244
You should come down sometime
after you're done fixing Evangeline.

674
00:38:09.036 --> 00:38:11.580
Uh… it's my grandmother's name.

675
00:38:11.664 --> 00:38:13.124
-Ah.
-Yeah.

676
00:38:13.207 --> 00:38:16.669
I have a whole lot of cars.
but she's my favorite.

677
00:38:17.211 --> 00:38:19.005
I guess I'm sentimental that way. huh?

678
00:38:19.630 --> 00:38:20.965
Right. Sure.

679
00:38:21.465 --> 00:38:24.260
I'll. uh… I'll do my best.

680
00:38:24.844 --> 00:38:25.886
Tony said.

681
00:38:37.315 --> 00:38:39.191
<i>♪ Every night… ♪</i>

682
00:38:39.275 --> 00:38:42.862
Parker. Benny. Jordan.
can you come down here. please?

683
00:38:42.945 --> 00:38:44.238
Okay. I'm coming!

684
00:38:44.322 --> 00:38:46.574
Hey. Nathan. you busy?

685
00:38:47.491 --> 00:38:48.784
<i>♪ In my head ♪</i>

686
00:38:48.868 --> 00:38:50.202
<i>♪ Do they care? ♪</i>

687
00:38:50.286 --> 00:38:52.997
<i>♪ Do they ever even wonder? ♪</i>

688
00:38:53.831 --> 00:38:55.416
<i>♪ Do they wonder? ♪</i>

689
00:38:55.499 --> 00:38:56.917
Hi. honey.

690
00:38:57.001 --> 00:38:58.794
<i>♪ Open up the door</i>
<i>And let your darkness… ♪</i>

691
00:38:58.878 --> 00:39:00.504
What are you guys doing here?

692
00:39:01.297 --> 00:39:03.674
Is everything okay? What's going on?

693
00:39:03.758 --> 00:39:04.842
We're gonna fix the fence.

694
00:39:05.426 --> 00:39:06.344
Come on.

695
00:39:06.427 --> 00:39:08.512
You don't have to do
everything on your own. Mom.

696
00:39:08.596 --> 00:39:09.889
Yeah. we wanted to help.

697
00:39:09.972 --> 00:39:11.599
And we brought hot chocolate and pastries.

698
00:39:13.017 --> 00:39:14.143
Who needs gloves?

699
00:39:14.226 --> 00:39:15.936
I never forget my gloves.

700
00:39:18.939 --> 00:39:22.068
All right. I'll supervise pastries
while they fix the fence.

701
00:39:22.151 --> 00:39:23.277
Your favorite.

702
00:39:23.361 --> 00:39:25.821
<i>♪ The people. the people… ♪</i>

703
00:39:25.905 --> 00:39:26.864
Hot chocolate!

704
00:39:26.947 --> 00:39:29.283
- Don't eat the whole thing.
- It's so hot

705
00:39:34.288 --> 00:39:35.956
Who wants one? Hot chocolate?

706
00:39:42.421 --> 00:39:43.589
Oh. thank you.

707
00:39:45.341 --> 00:39:47.343
You know you didn't have to do this.

708
00:39:47.426 --> 00:39:48.552
Yes. we did.

709
00:39:49.053 --> 00:39:50.137
You're the best.

710
00:39:56.060 --> 00:39:57.978
Wait. Did you…

711
00:39:58.062 --> 00:39:58.979
No.

712
00:40:04.026 --> 00:40:05.820
-Oh my God.
-Hello.

713
00:40:06.320 --> 00:40:07.863
- Dad!
- Hello!

714
00:40:08.948 --> 00:40:10.241
Gentle! Gentle!

715
00:40:14.453 --> 00:40:15.746
- Hey.
- Hi.

716
00:40:15.830 --> 00:40:17.039
Hi.

717
00:40:18.040 --> 00:40:20.793
-What are you doing here?
-Dr. Segil said I could go home.

718
00:40:20.876 --> 00:40:23.838
So I called Will
and wanted to surprise everyone.

719
00:40:33.472 --> 00:40:35.724
Come on. Bring it in. Bring it in.

720
00:40:42.481 --> 00:40:43.691
Okay.

721
00:40:46.193 --> 00:40:47.361
Thank you.

722
00:40:47.945 --> 00:40:49.613
- Can I get you anything else?
- No.

723
00:40:49.697 --> 00:40:52.241
No. I am all set. Thank you.

724
00:40:52.324 --> 00:40:55.870
I mean. Katherine brought me enough
blankets to host a slumber party. so…

725
00:40:56.954 --> 00:40:57.997
Um…

726
00:40:59.290 --> 00:41:03.544
I'm really sorry that I didn't come
to see you at the hospital.

727
00:41:03.627 --> 00:41:05.254
After what happened to you.

728
00:41:05.754 --> 00:41:08.716
I can't imagine you want
to spend one more minute in a hospital.

729
00:41:08.799 --> 00:41:10.968
So you do not owe me an apology.

730
00:41:11.969 --> 00:41:13.637
Oh. and I loved the smoothies.

731
00:41:14.138 --> 00:41:16.223
-You did?
-I love that you made 'em for me.

732
00:41:16.307 --> 00:41:18.476
So thank you.

733
00:41:19.477 --> 00:41:21.479
Hey. Jackie. listen. Um…

734
00:41:22.146 --> 00:41:24.231
This has been so hard on all of us.

735
00:41:24.732 --> 00:41:27.818
Don't waste another second
feeling guilty. all right?

736
00:41:27.902 --> 00:41:30.321
We all just need to get back to living

737
00:41:30.905 --> 00:41:34.825
in the moment
and… and definitely with no regrets.

738
00:41:35.367 --> 00:41:36.243
Okay?

739
00:41:50.382 --> 00:41:51.217
Hi.

740
00:41:57.806 --> 00:42:00.267
That was a… good thing you did before.

741
00:42:00.351 --> 00:42:01.227
For my mom.

742
00:42:01.310 --> 00:42:04.688
Yeah. well. we've all been so distant.

743
00:42:05.189 --> 00:42:07.066
I think we needed
to spend some time together.

744
00:42:07.566 --> 00:42:09.401
You know. like… like. really together.

745
00:42:12.196 --> 00:42:15.616
Yeah. Well… it worked.

746
00:42:16.200 --> 00:42:20.579
Yeah. and now that your dad's home.
maybe we can all go back to normal.

747
00:42:22.414 --> 00:42:24.667
Yeah. Maybe.

748
00:42:25.793 --> 00:42:27.836
Are you busy?

749
00:42:29.588 --> 00:42:33.259
Um… not anymore.

750
00:42:35.052 --> 00:42:36.011
Would you come with me?

751
00:42:36.512 --> 00:42:39.223
Um… sure.

752
00:42:49.066 --> 00:42:50.442
What are we doing here?

753
00:42:50.943 --> 00:42:51.902
You'll see.

754
00:43:02.621 --> 00:43:04.164
What… what's going on?

755
00:43:06.417 --> 00:43:08.168
Why… why are we here?

756
00:43:09.837 --> 00:43:10.921
Do you remember?

757
00:43:11.422 --> 00:43:13.716
You brought me here
when I needed somewhere to go.

758
00:43:14.675 --> 00:43:16.343
Of course I remember.

759
00:43:17.303 --> 00:43:19.805
We've been so wrapped up in things lately.

760
00:43:20.306 --> 00:43:22.933
you know. with your dad
and with what happened. I…

761
00:43:23.517 --> 00:43:27.146
I wanted to bring you somewhere beautiful.
somewhere that meant something.

762
00:43:29.857 --> 00:43:32.651
I know you're trying
to make me feel better.

763
00:43:33.986 --> 00:43:35.738
And I know what we said.

764
00:43:36.238 --> 00:43:38.949
but I can't do this with you.

765
00:43:40.075 --> 00:43:41.952
I don't want to be friends.

766
00:43:44.246 --> 00:43:45.956
I don't want to be friends either.

767
00:43:47.249 --> 00:43:48.125
What?

768
00:43:49.376 --> 00:43:51.295
I know I said that we couldn't

769
00:43:51.378 --> 00:43:55.924
and that it wasn't the right time before.
but now might be all that we have.

770
00:43:56.008 --> 00:43:57.760
<i>♪ I've been chasing this for years ♪</i>

771
00:43:57.843 --> 00:43:59.053
<i>♪ My legs don't work… ♪</i>

